// CotSC: English translation extracted from bg0607_flaming_fist_gaol.d
// Original English strings preserved exactly. Translate text inside ~...~ only.

@1 = ~I see you gawking at me, Rivvin. You're lucky I am behind these bars cause otherwise you'd end up just like my neighbour. With your own eyes forcefully shoved down your throat.~
@2 = ~Pitiful sight indeed. You chose to throw away your freedom by giving in to your impulses. In a way we are alike in that regard. Although I chose to assimilate to life on the surface and abandon ways of the Underdark.~
@3 = ~We are superior to surface-dwellers. Our intelligence, our culture. Our path is open only to the strong and wicked. You betrayed those ideals by forming alliance with the enemies of the dark.~
@4 = ~I fled the Underdark because I grew skeptical of the rituals upheld by the priestesses. They serve little meaningful purpose and to what end? To satisfy a selfish goddess who would leave us for granted had opportunity arised? I was blinded by drow ideals and culture but with patience and persistence I sought reason. Reason to leave our traditions and customs behind. The darkness that inhabits each of us will always remain, undoubtedly, but we all forge our own destiny.~
@5 = ~There is some wisdom in your words. Accepting it would require me to lose the part of me that made me a drow. I did choose a life on the surface because I faced being turned into a Drider otherwise. I didn't settle in Baldur's Gate out of my own volition, but rather out of lack of alternatives. I couldn't accept people's kindness and charity. It makes me sick to my stomach… so I killed an annoying neighbour who eyeballed me one second too long.~
@6 = ~You and I both experienced extreme racial prejudice and our time on the surface hasn't been easy, but there is a thin line between arrogance and stupidity. One can be unhappy and drained from dealing with this accursed sun, whilst also choosing to ignore it and adapt, whilst other can be just as frustrated and let it all out physically, like you demonstrated. Look where you are… condemned to a cell, awaiting execution for murder.~
@7 = ~I... I see. You are acting a lot like a Rivvin but... I let my nature get the best of me. And now I suffer the consequences when I could pull myself together and ignore my internal desire to kill.~
@8 = ~You have little time to think about it now. I wish you would understand much sooner. May Shar guide you and allow you to avoid Lolth's vengeance.~
@9 = ~Pitiful look of a drow stuck in a cell. You are getting exactly what you deserve. If only the rest of your vile, permeated with evil kind could suffer the same grim fate.~
@10 = ~You committed a murder and you're still ranting and threatening? Funny, considering we are on this side of the cell, and you're all the way in there.~
@11 = ~I respect the zeal and vigour but that's what got you in here in the first place. Should've thought your murder scheme more cautiously, not to get caught.~
@12 = ~Brrr… seeing that coldness and malevolence in his eyes is enough to make your hair white.~
@13 = ~If that is all, walk away, rivvin.~
@14 = ~Salutations. I am the High Constable of the City Watch. How can I help you?~
@15 = ~What does a High Constable do?~
@16 = ~We are looking for Eltan.~
@17 = ~Goodbye.~
@18 = ~I am responsible for appointing members of the Watch - a voluntary group of citizens who enforce the law after completing a special training. They aid Flaming Fist forces by patrolling the streets, reporting crimes or intervening themselves. They are a tremendous support in dealing with thievery and other awful crimes within the walls of the city. Anyone can volunteer as long as they are the citizen of Baldur's Gate.~
@19 = ~He's either upstairs or retired to the palace. Either way, try not to linger here if you don't need to. You can always return later and check again.~
@20 = ~Are they gone? The slimes?~
@21 = ~Yes. They are gone.~
@22 = ~Nope. They are still down there.~
@23 = ~Thank goodness! I've had enough of those dreadful things. I'll be on my way before any more appear.~
@24 = ~Still there? Then this is no place for me! I'll find somewhere safer to wait.~
